// Phase 10 Plan 3 (D-10-14): the discriminating per-path-borrow fixture's
// CALLEE half. Two arms diverge in borrow behavior -- On creates a genuine
// borrow of its own parameter and returns it; Off takes (owns) it instead
// -- a PER-PATH divergence a per-function contract hop
// (peerLoanCarryFact.ReturnsBorrowOfParam, corevalidate_peer_liveness.go)
// cannot express, since that fact is declared once for the whole function.
//
// This function is deliberately NEVER CALLED from within this same checked
// program: this exact shape (a match-bodied function with an undeclared
// return type whose arms disagree on whether the return carries a live
// borrow) is check.Program's own D-07-33/PublishProblemsFor
// core.origin_omitted class, exactly like the pre-existing
// public_view_multi_arm_omitted.lang precedent -- `lang check` accepts the
// DECLARATION unconditionally (check.Program never validates origin, only
// `lang interface export` would), but a match-bodied function's declared
// return type cannot ITSELF carry a borrow(...) annotation at all this
// phase (ownership.match_borrowed_return_unsupported), so this shape can
// never be made Callable (SEM-06) by declaring around the omission either.
// The plan's own action text anticipates exactly this: "If the current
// grammar cannot express a two-path callee with that shape ... fall back to
// a checked-core construction built by the same pipeline from the closest
// expressible source." pathoracle_test.go's
// TestCompositionDiscriminatesPerPathBorrow does exactly that: this file is
// checked through the real syntax.Parse -> check.Program pipeline entirely
// on its own to obtain a genuine, pipeline-produced core.Function for
// `callee`, and compose_per_path_borrow_caller_accept.lang (checked
// separately, calling a genuinely Callable pass-through instead) supplies
// the CALLER half; the test stitches the caller's own OpCall.CalleeID onto
// this callee's real ID before driving both through
// pathoracle.RecomputeEndpoints -- pathoracle itself never consults
// Callable at all, only the typed core artifact.

module phase10.compose_per_path_borrow_callee

export {
  fn callee
}

data Switch =
  | On
  | Off

fn callee(flag: Switch) -> Switch {
  match flag {
    On => {
      let held = borrow flag
      held
    }
    Off => {
      let taken = take flag
      taken
    }
  }
}
